 ### [Multi-Identity Embedding](16787-multi-identity-embedding.md)
-Multi-Identity Embedding is a method for identifying contributing users in collaborative Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) training by embedding customized hidden information about specific clusters of training views. It solves the problem of scalable attribution in multi-user scenarios by allowing a single NeRF model to hide distinct identities for different spatial regions without requiring model retraining for each new watermark. Unlike prior approaches that embed only a single global watermark, this method isolates identity information to specific clusters of anchor views, maintaining high visual quality by preventing false positives for unmarked identities. See [Multi-Identity Embedding](16787-multi-identity-embedding.md).
+Multi-Identity Embedding identifies contributing users in collaborative NeRF training by embedding customized hidden information about specific clusters of training views. It solves scalable attribution in multi-user scenarios by allowing a single NeRF model to hide distinct identities for different spatial regions without requiring model retraining for each new watermark. Unlike prior approaches that embed only a single global watermark, this method isolates identity information to specific clusters of anchor views, maintaining high visual quality by preventing false positives for unmarked identities. Choose this variant when attributing contributions from multiple distinct users in a shared cultural landmark reconstruction pipeline. See [Multi-Identity Embedding](16787-multi-identity-embedding.md).
 
